{"y":2018,"label":"2017–18","coach":"Kevin Ollie","conf":"AAC","confShort":"AAC","w":14,"l":18,"cw":7,"cl":11,"confFinish":"8th in AAC","finish":"none","srs":1.08,"sos":6.05,"ortg":99.9,"drtg":107.2,"pace":67.1,"ppg":68.2,"oppg":73.1,"story":{"headline":"The Nadir","text":"The bottom. UConn was unranked all season and absorbed 11 double-digit losses. In January 2018 the school revealed the NCAA was investigating possible recruiting violations, and home attendance sank to its lowest level in nearly 30 years. The Huskies finished 7–11 in the AAC and lost to SMU 80–73 in the first round of the conference tournament on March 8; two days later, Kevin Ollie was fired for just cause. Jalen Adams (18.1 points, 4.7 assists) made second-team All-AAC, and sophomore Christian Vital scored a career-high 30 in an 85–66 win over Boston University. In July 2019 the NCAA vacated the season's wins because of the recruiting violations, leaving an official record of 0–18 — and a program in need of a reset.","moments":[{"date":"2018-03-10","title":"Ollie fired","text":"Two days after the season ends, UConn fires Kevin Ollie for just cause amid an NCAA investigation."}],"sources":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2017%E2%80%9318_UConn_Huskies_men's_basketball_team","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/UConn_Huskies_men%27s_basketball","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kevin_Ollie","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jalen_Adams"]},"roster":[{"pid":"jalen-adams-2","name":"Jalen Adams","num":"4","cls":"JR","pos":"G","ht":"6-3","wt":195,"home":"Roxbury, MA","hs":"Brewster Academy","rsci":"20 ( 2015 )","photo":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/headshots/mens-college-basketball/players/full/3934622.png","pg":{"g":30,"gs":30,"mp":38.1,"pts":18.1,"trb":4.2,"ast":4.7,"stl":1.5,"blk":0.3,"tov":2.9,"fg_pct":0.43,"fg3_pct":0.324,"ft_pct":0.796,"orb":0.9,"pf":1.5},"tot":{"mp":1144,"fg":208,"fga":484,"fg3":48,"fg3a":148,"ft":78,"fta":98,"orb":26,"drb":101,"trb":127,"ast":141,"stl":46,"blk":10,"tov":87,"pf":46,"pts":542,"g":3